abstract: >
  A Python library and research methodology for stating formal
  correspondences between mathematical models across domains
  (dynamical systems, information theory including directed
  information / information flow, thermodynamics, viability theory),
  each backed by an independently reproducible verification suite.
  Includes typed scope/composition contracts, exact interval and
  identifiability certificates, finite causal abstraction and transport,
  weighted conformal calibration, and synthetic measurement-model pilots
  (muonium gravity, adaptive modular networks) with separated evidence
  and empirical-status reporting.
  Developed with AI assistance (implementation and verification by
  Claude; external reviews by Astra).
